{
  "//": [
    "The support tier as data: which e2e suite builds which dial cell.",
    "",
    "Each row says that one suite under tests/e2e/ scaffolds the cell, as",
    "`keel.dials` settles it, and builds it with its real toolchain. Every",
    "dial is spelled out, the defaults among them, so a default that moves",
    "never moves a claim. `singles` are single-service cells; `products`",
    "are product cells, each naming the services its suite compiles",
    "(`builds`). The suite fakes the build of the others.",
    "",
    "A cell no row names can still be first-class. The rules in",
    "`support-tier.ts` read a cell without the agent harness as its twin",
    "with it (P1), and a product's service as any service with the same",
    "bytes (P2). Every other cell keel offers is best-effort. A suite name",
    "is provenance, for the docs: nothing at run time resolves it.",
    "",
    "`support-tier.ts` validates this file at load.",
    "`tests/support-tier.test.ts` holds it to `tests/e2e/`, the CI shard",
    "matrix and the paths golden, and `tests/support-tier.premises.test.ts`",
    "holds P1 and P2 on every cell. A new e2e suite that builds a cell as",
    "keel scaffolds it adds its row here in the same change. One that",
    "proves no cell declares its role in `tests/support/e2e-roles.ts`."
  ],
